
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

# 1. Load Dataset
df = pd.read_csv("City_day.csv")

# 2. Display Dataset Information
print("First 5 Records:")
print(df.head())

print("\nDataset Shape:")
print(df.shape)

print("\nColumn Names:")
print(df.columns.tolist())

print("\nDataset Information:")
df.info()

print("\nMissing Values:")
print(df.isnull().sum())

# 3. Convert Date Column
df["Date"] = pd.to_datetime(
    df["Date"],
    format="%Y-%m-%d"
)

# 4. Summary Statistics
print("\nSummary Statistics:")
print(df.describe())

# 5. AQI Trend Line Graph
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))
plt.plot(df["Date"], df["AQI"], marker="o")
plt.title("AQI Trend Over Time")
plt.xlabel("Date")
plt.ylabel("AQI")
plt.xticks(rotation=45)
plt.grid(True)
plt.show()

# 6. Pollutant Levels Line Graph
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))
plt.plot(df["Date"], df["PM2.5"], label="PM2.5")
plt.plot(df["Date"], df["PM10"], label="PM10")
plt.plot(df["Date"], df["CO"], label="CO")
plt.title("Pollutant Levels Over Time")
plt.xlabel("Date")
plt.ylabel("Pollutant Level")
plt.legend()
plt.xticks(rotation=45)
plt.grid(True)
plt.show()

# 7. Bar Graph
plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))
plt.bar(df["Date"], df["AQI"])
plt.title("AQI Comparison by Date")
plt.xlabel("Date")
plt.ylabel("AQI")
plt.xticks(rotation=45)
plt.show()

# 8. Box Plot
plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))
plt.boxplot(df["AQI"].dropna())
plt.title("AQI Distribution")
plt.ylabel("AQI")
plt.show()

# 9. Scatter Plot: PM2.5 vs AQI
plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))
plt.scatter(df["PM2.5"], df["AQI"])
plt.title("PM2.5 vs AQI")
plt.xlabel("PM2.5")
plt.ylabel("AQI")
plt.grid(True)
plt.show()

# 10. Scatter Plot: PM10 vs AQI
plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))
plt.scatter(df["PM10"], df["AQI"])
plt.title("PM10 vs AQI")
plt.xlabel("PM10")
plt.ylabel("AQI")
plt.grid(True)
plt.show()

# 11. Scatter Plot: CO vs AQI
plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))
plt.scatter(df["CO"], df["AQI"])
plt.title("CO vs AQI")
plt.xlabel("CO")
plt.ylabel("AQI")
plt.grid(True)
plt.show()



Explanation
1. Import Libraries: Pandas is used for data handling and Matplotlib is used to create graphs.

2. Load Dataset: read_csv() loads the air pollution dataset.

3. Display Data: head(), shape and columns display the first five records, dataset size and column names.

4. Dataset Information: info() displays column details and data types.

5. Check Missing Values: isnull().sum() checks missing values in each column.

6. Convert Date: to_datetime() converts the Date column into date format.

7. Summary Statistics: describe() displays count, mean, minimum, maximum and other statistical values.

8. Line Graph: plot() displays the AQI trend over time.

9. Pollutant Graph: Displays PM2.5, PM10 and CO levels over time.

10. Bar Graph: bar() compares AQI values for different dates.

11. Box Plot: boxplot() displays the distribution of AQI and helps identify outliers.

12. Scatter Plots: scatter() shows the relationship between PM2.5, PM10, CO and AQI.
3. Conclusion
Successfully analyzed air pollution data and visualized AQI and pollutant levels using different graphs in Matplotlib.
4. Important Functions
Function	Purpose
read_csv()	Load CSV file
head()	Display first 5 records
shape	Display rows and columns
info()	Display dataset information
isnull()	Check missing values
to_datetime()	Convert date format
describe()	Calculate summary statistics
plot()	Create line graph
bar()	Create bar graph
boxplot()	Create box plot
scatter()	Create scatter plot
show()	Display graph
legend()	Display graph labels
